    "locator": "HV (CE) 46–48; 55–56; 61–63; 76; 85–86",
    "statement": "Viṣṇu resolves to descend; Kṛṣṇa is born to Devakī as Yaśodā bears a daughter (48.11), grows up in Vraja, subdues Kāliya (55–56), lifts Govardhana (61–62), sports at night with the cowherd women (63.24–35), kills Kaṃsa (76) and founds Dvārakā (85–86): the first connected childhood narrative.",
